export const FINISHED_LESSON_MD: Record<string, string> = {"s0-u1-l01":"# Greetings & \"How are you?\"\n\n**Empire English** · Stage 0 — **Recruit** (Pre-A1 → A1) · Unit 1 · **Lesson 1**\n⏱️ ~30 min · 📹 Recorded + live · Prerequisite: Unit 0\n*Built from: `curriculum/stage0/unit1-introducing-yourself.md` · **S0-U1-L01***\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **At a glance (~30 min):** Warm-up 3 · Input 6 · Decode 5 · Accent Lab 4 · Train 6 · Your Turn 4 · Orders 1 · Review 1.\n> **Objectives:** greet by time of day · ask/answer *How are you?* · say goodbye.\n> **Support:** allow just *Hi* + *I'm fine* for the anxious beginner. **Stretch:** add *Nice to meet you.* / *Have a nice day!*\n> **Big picture:** first real lesson after sounds — set a warm, \"you-can-do-this\" tone. Everything here is FIXED phrases; resist teaching grammar deeply (that's L02).\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Your Conquest — هدفك من الدرس\nBy the end of this lesson, **you'll be able to:**\n- Greet people in English **at any time of day**.\n- Ask **\"How are you?\"** and answer it.\n- Say **goodbye** politely.\n\n> في آخر الدرس هتقدر تسلّم بالإنجليزي في أي وقت في اليوم، تسأل الشخص **\"How are you?\"** وترد عليه، وتقول باي بشكل مؤدب. 👑\n\n---\n\n## 👑 Why this matters — ليه ده مهم\nأي محادثة إنجليزي في الدنيا بتبدأ بالتحية. لو اتقنت الجزء الصغير ده، هتدخل أي كلام وانت واثق في نفسك. ده أول لبنة في الـ Empire بتاعتك — **لبنة كل يوم، والإمبراطورية بتتبني.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Warm-up — سخّن (افتكر)\nافتكر من **Unit 0**: قول اسمك + جملة نجاة واحدة اتعلمتها (زي *\"Nice to meet you\"* أو *\"Can you repeat, please?\"*).\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~3 min.** Fast round: each learner says their name + one Unit-0 survival phrase. Retrieval only — keep it warm and quick; don't correct much here.\n\n---\n\n## 👂 Watch & Listen — اسمع وشوف\nشوف/اسمع المحادثتين دول (فيه فيديو في المنصة 📹). ركّز على **\"How are you?\"** والرد عليها.\n\n**Dialogue 1 — in the morning**\n> **A:** Good morning! How are you?\n> **B:** I'm fine, thanks. And you?\n> **A:** I'm great, thanks!\n\n**Dialogue 2 — in the evening**\n> **A:** Hi, good evening!\n> **B:** Hello! Not bad, thanks. And you?\n> **A:** I'm good. See you!\n\n**الترجمة (gloss):**\n\n| English | بالعربي |\n|---|---|\n| Good morning | صباح الخير |\n| How are you? | إزيك؟ / عامل إيه؟ |\n| I'm fine, thanks | أنا كويس، شكرًا |\n| And you? | وانت؟ |\n| Not bad | مش بطّال |\n| See you! | أشوفك بعدين! |\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~6 min.** Play the model **twice** — first for gist, second time learners underline *How are you?* + the answers. Stress that these are **fixed phrases**: we don't translate them word-by-word.\n\n---\n\n## 🧩 Decode it — القاعدة (افهمها صح)\n\n**1) التحية حسب الوقت — greetings by time of day:**\n\n| الوقت | English greeting |\n|---|---|\n| الصبح (لحد ~12 الضهر) | **Good morning** |\n| بعد الضهر (~12 → 6) | **Good afternoon** |\n| بالليل (بعد ~6) | **Good evening** |\n| أي وقت (غير رسمي) | **Hi / Hello** |\n\n**2) How are you? + الردود:**\n- السؤال: **How are you?** = إزيك؟\n- الردود (من الأحسن للعادي): **I'm great / I'm good / I'm fine / Not bad**, thanks. **And you?**\n\n> ⚠️ ملاحظة مهمة: بنقول **I'm** (اختصار لـ *I am*) قبل الحالة → *I'm fine.* ✅ — مش *\"I fine\"* ❌\n> (الـ *to be* = فعل الكينونة، هنشتغل عليها أكتر في الدرس الجاي — دلوقتي احفظها كجملة جاهزة.)\n\n**3) الوداع — saying goodbye:** **Goodbye · Bye · See you · See you later.**\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~5 min, in Arabic.** Teach the time table, then drill *How are you?* + the four answers. **Watch for:** learners dropping the verb (*\"I fine\"*) — fix the *I'm* now. Don't over-explain *to be*; it's L02. Note the friendly, non-formal use of *Hi/Hello* anytime.\n\n---\n\n## 🗡️ Your Arsenal — ذخيرتك من الكلمات\n\n| English | بالعربي | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| hello / hi | أهلاً / هاي | *Hi! How are you?* |\n| good morning / afternoon / evening | صباح/مساء الخير | *Good evening, everyone.* |\n| fine / good / great | كويس / تمام / عظيم | *I'm great, thanks.* |\n| not bad | مش بطّال | *Not bad, and you?* |\n| thanks | شكرًا | *I'm fine, thanks.* |\n| goodbye / bye / see you | مع السلامة / باي / أشوفك | *Bye! See you later.* |\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Accent Lab — معمل النطق\n\n**Target sound: the /h/ in *hello* and *how*.**\nالعربي أحيانًا بيبلع الـ /h/ في أول الكلمة. لازم تنطقها **واضحة** — زي \"هـ\" قوية شوية.\n\n- **Feel it:** حط إيدك قدام بقّك — المفروض تحس بنفخة هوا خفيفة مع **h**ello و **h**ow.\n- **Hear the difference:** *ello ❌ → **h**ello ✅* · *ow ❌ → **h**ow ✅*\n\n**Intonation — الموسيقى:** *\"How are you?\"* بتطلع بنبرة **صاعدة وودودة ↗**، والرد *\"I'm fine, thanks\"* بينزل **↘**.\n\n> 🎧 **Record & compare:** قول *\"Good morning! How are you?\"* → اسمع النموذج → قارن الـ /h/ بتاعتك ونبرتك الودودة. أعِد لحد ما تقرّب من النموذج.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Drill /h/ (hello, how, here, happy). **Watch for:** dropped /h/ (very common). Model the rising-then-falling melody of *How are you? → I'm fine, thanks*; have them exaggerate the friendly tone first, then bring it to natural.\n\n---\n\n## 🏋️ Train — تدرّب\n\n**Exercise 1 — Choose the right greeting (حسب الوقت):**\n1. 8:00 الصبح → Good __________\n2. 3:00 بعد الضهر → Good __________\n3. 8:00 بالليل → Good __________\n\n**Exercise 2 — Complete the conversation:**\n> A: Hi! How ______ you?\n> B: I'm ______, thanks. And ______?\n> A: I'm great!\n\n**Exercise 3 — Match:**\n\n| # | English | | بالعربي / الرد |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | How are you? | → | a. Bye! See you! |\n| 2 | Goodbye | → | b. صباح الخير |\n| 3 | Good morning | → | c. I'm fine, thanks |\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~6 min.** Individually, then pair-check.\n> **Answers — Ex1:** morning · afternoon · evening. **Ex2:** are · fine (or good/great) · you. **Ex3:** 1→c · 2→a · 3→b.\n\n---\n\n## 🎤 Your Turn — دورك\n\nاعمل محادثة تحية **كاملة** مع زميل (أو سجّل لوحدك):\n1. سلّم حسب الوقت **دلوقتي** (Good morning / afternoon / evening).\n2. اسأل: **How are you?**\n3. رد + اسأل تاني: **I'm …, thanks. And you?**\n4. قول باي: **See you!**\n\n> 🎙️ **Record one greeting exchange and keep it.** ده أول \"before\" clip في رحلتك — هنقارنه بصوتك بعد كام أسبوع. 👑\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Pairs greet for the **current** time of day; swap roles; each records one exchange.\n> **Success check:** learner performs a full greeting exchange **intelligibly**, with an audible **/h/** and a **friendly tone**.\n\n---\n\n## 📜 Your Orders — مهمتك\n- **النهاردة:** سلّم على حد بالإنجليزي — في الحقيقة أو في رسالة.\n- **Post a voice note** in the community: a greeting + *\"How are you?\"* + your answer.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Remember — افتكر\n- Greetings by time: **morning / afternoon / evening**.\n- **How are you? → I'm fine, thanks. And you?**\n- انطق الـ **/h/** بوضوح، وخلي نبرتك **ودودة**.\n- *(هترجع التحيات دي في كل warm-up جاي — spaced review.)*\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Self-check — صحّح لنفسك\n- **Ex1:** 1) morning · 2) afternoon · 3) evening\n- **Ex2:** are · fine / good / great · you\n- **Ex3:** 1→c · 2→a · 3→b\n\n---\n\n*Empire English 👑 — الاستمرار أهم من الشدّة. Consistency beats intensity. لبنة كل يوم.*\n","s0-u1-l02":"# \"Hello, I'm…\" — Saying Who You Are\n\n**Empire English** · Stage 0 — **Recruit** (Pre-A1 → A1) · Unit 1 · **Lesson 2**\n⏱️ ~30 min · 📹 Recorded + live · Prerequisite: L01\n*Built from: `curriculum/stage0/unit1-introducing-yourself.md` · **S0-U1-L02***\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **At a glance (~30 min):** Warm-up 3 · Input 7 · Decode 5 · Accent Lab 4 · Train 6 · Your Turn 3 · Orders 1 · Review 1.\n> **Objectives:** introduce yourself (name · country · job) · ask *What's your name?* · record a first self-intro.\n> **Support:** give the full written frames + let them re-listen. **Stretch:** add *I live in…*.\n> **Big picture:** this is the emotional \"I can introduce myself in English!\" win. Warmth first, accuracy second.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Your Conquest — هدفك من الدرس\nBy the end, **you'll be able to:**\n- Introduce yourself with your **name, country, and job**.\n- Ask **\"What's your name?\"** and answer.\n- **Record your first spoken self-introduction.** 🎙️\n\n> في آخر الدرس هتقدّم نفسك بالإنجليزي — اسمك، بلدك، وشغلك — وتسأل حد عن اسمه، وتسجّل أول تعريف بنفسك.\n\n---\n\n## 👑 Why this matters — ليه ده مهم\nلما حد يسألك *\"Tell me about yourself\"* في مقابلة شغل أو أول ما تقابل حد جديد — دي أول حاجة محتاج تتقنها. النهاردة بتبني اللبنة دي.\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Warm-up — سخّن (افتكر)\nافتكر من L01: سلّم حسب الوقت + اسأل **How are you?** ورد.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~3 min.** Quick greeting round (from L01), for the current time of day.\n\n---\n\n## 👂 Watch & Listen — اسمع وشوف\nشوف/اسمع 3 تعريفات قصيرة (فيه فيديو في المنصة 📹):\n\n> **1.** Hello! My name is Omar. I'm from Egypt. I'm a teacher.\n> **2.** Hi, I'm Mariam. I'm from Egypt, and I'm a nurse.\n> **3.** Hello, I'm Khaled. I'm an engineer.\n\n**الترجمة (gloss):**\n\n| English | بالعربي |\n|---|---|\n| My name is… / I'm… | اسمي… / أنا… |\n| I'm from… | أنا من… |\n| I'm a / an … (+ job) | أنا (وظيفة) |\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~7 min.** Play twice. Learners notice the three \"building blocks\": *My name is… / I'm from… / I'm a…*. Point out *I'm* = *I am* (fixed).\n\n---\n\n## 🧩 Decode it — القاعدة (افهمها صح)\nعشان تعرّف نفسك، بتستخدم **3 لبنات**:\n\n| # | Frame | مثال |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **My name is ___** (أو **I'm ___**) | *My name is Omar.* / *I'm Omar.* |\n| 2 | **I'm from ___** (البلد) | *I'm from Egypt.* |\n| 3 | **I'm a / an ___** (الوظيفة) | *I'm a teacher.* |\n\n> ⚠️ لازم تقول **I'm** (= I am) → *I'm a teacher.* ✅ — مش *\"I teacher\"* ❌.\n> ده الفعل **to be** (فعل الكينونة) — أهم فعل في الإنجليزي، وهنستخدمه طول الوقت.\n\n**السؤال:** *What's your name?* = اسمك إيه؟ → *My name is… / I'm…*\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~5 min, in Arabic.** Teach the 3 frames. **Watch for:** the dropped verb (*\"I teacher\"*, *\"I from Egypt\"*) — this is THE error to fix now. Drill *I'm* every time. Keep *a/an* light (full treatment is L04).\n\n---\n\n## 🗡️ Your Arsenal — ذخيرتك من الكلمات\n\n| English | بالعربي | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| My name is… / I'm… | اسمي… / أنا… | *I'm Sara.* |\n| I'm from… | أنا من… | *I'm from Egypt.* |\n| teacher / engineer / doctor | مدرّس / مهندس / دكتور | *I'm a doctor.* |\n| student / nurse / driver | طالب / ممرضة / سواق | *I'm a student.* |\n| What's your name? | اسمك إيه؟ | *— What's your name? — I'm Ali.* |\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Accent Lab — معمل النطق\n**Target: the /aɪ/ in *I* and the clear /m/ in *I'm*.**\n- *I* بتتنطق **/aɪ/** (زي \"آي\") — مش \"إي\".\n- في *I'm*، اقفل شفايفك على الـ **/m/** بوضوح: *I'm* (آيم).\n- **Stress the key word:** *\"I'm a **TEA**cher.\"* (الضغط على الوظيفة).\n\n> 🎧 **Record & compare:** قول *\"I → I'm → I'm a teacher.\"* → اسمع النموذج → قارن الـ /aɪ/ والـ /m/ والضغط.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Build it up: *I → I'm → I'm a teacher.* Watch for *I* said as \"ee\". Model sentence stress on the job word.\n\n---\n\n## 🏋️ Train — تدرّب\n\n**Exercise 1 — Fill the frames (بمعلوماتك الحقيقية):**\n1. My name is __________.\n2. I'm from __________.\n3. I'm a/an __________.\n\n**Exercise 2 — Fix the mistake (صلّح الغلط):**\n1. ❌ *I teacher.* → ✅ __________\n2. ❌ *I from Egypt.* → ✅ __________\n3. ❌ *My name Omar.* → ✅ __________\n\n**Exercise 3 — Order the conversation (رتّب):**\n- ( ) I'm from Egypt.\n- ( ) Hi! What's your name?\n- ( ) I'm Mona. And you?\n- ( ) I'm Ahmed. Where are you from?\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~6 min.** Individually → pair-check.\n> **Answers — Ex2:** *I'm a teacher.* / *I'm from Egypt.* / *My name is Omar.*\n> **Ex3:** 2 – 1 – 3 – 4 order → \"Hi! What's your name?\" / \"I'm Mona. And you?\" / \"I'm Ahmed. Where are you from?\" / \"I'm from Egypt.\"\n\n---\n\n## 🎤 Your Turn — دورك\nسجّل تعريف بنفسك في **3 جمل** (بمعلوماتك الحقيقية):\n1. Greeting + name → *Hello, I'm ___.*\n2. Country → *I'm from ___.*\n3. Job → *I'm a/an ___.*\n\n> 🎙️ **Record your 3-sentence self-introduction and keep it.** ده جزء من الـ \"before\" بتاعك. 👑\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~3 min.** Everyone records a 3-sentence self-intro (real info).\n> **Success check:** 3 correct, intelligible self-intro sentences with *I'm* used correctly (rubric: Accuracy + Pronunciation + Fluency at A1).\n\n---\n\n## 📜 Your Orders — مهمتك\n- **Post a 20–30s self-introduction voice note** in the community: greeting + name + country + job.\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Remember — افتكر\n- The 3 building blocks: **My name is… / I'm from… / I'm a…**\n- Always use **I'm** (= I am). *I'm a teacher* ✅.\n- *(هيرجع في warm-up الدرس الجاي.)*\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Self-check — صحّح لنفسك\n- **Ex2:** *I'm a teacher.* · *I'm from Egypt.* · *My name is Omar.*\n- **Ex3:** \"Hi! What's your name?\" → \"I'm Mona. And you?\" → \"I'm Ahmed. Where are you from?\" → \"I'm from Egypt.\"\n\n---\n\n*Empire English 👑 — لبنة كل يوم. You just introduced yourself in English.*\n","s0-u1-l03":"# \"Where Are You From?\" — Countries & Nationalities\n\n**Empire English** · Stage 0 — **Recruit** (A1) · Unit 1 · **Lesson 3**\n⏱️ ~30 min · 📹 Recorded + live · Prerequisite: L02\n*Built from: `curriculum/stage0/unit1-introducing-yourself.md` · **S0-U1-L03***\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **At a glance (~30 min):** Warm-up 4 · Input 6 · Decode 6 · Accent Lab 4 · Train 5 · Your Turn 4 · Orders — · Review 1.\n> **Objectives:** ask/answer *Where are you from?* · name countries + one nationality · report *He's/She's from…*.\n> **Support:** just *I'm from ___*. **Stretch:** *I'm Egyptian, from Cairo.*\n> **Note:** Arabic support eases to ~60% this lesson (the fade begins within the unit).\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Your Conquest — هدفك\nBy the end, **you'll be able to:**\n- Ask and answer **\"Where are you from?\"**\n- Name several **countries** (and say you're **Egyptian**).\n- Talk about someone else: **\"He's from Egypt.\"**\n\n> هتسأل وترد على *\"Where are you from?\"*، وتسمّي كذا بلد، وتتكلم عن حد تاني: *He's from Egypt.*\n\n---\n\n## 👑 Why this matters — ليه ده مهم\nسؤال *\"Where are you from?\"* بييجي في أول أي محادثة مع أجنبي. لبنة تانية في التعريف بنفسك.\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Warm-up — سخّن (افتكر)\nافتكر من L02: عرّف نفسك (name + job) في جملتين.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Rapid recall: 2–3 learners give their L02 self-intro (name + job).\n\n---\n\n## 👂 Watch & Listen — اسمع وشوف\n> **A:** Hi! Where are you from?\n> **B:** I'm from Egypt. And you?\n> **A:** I'm from Saudi Arabia.\n> **B:** This is Layla. **She's** from the UAE.\n\n**Countries (gloss):**\n\n| English | بالعربي |\n|---|---|\n| Egypt | مصر |\n| Saudi Arabia | السعودية |\n| the UAE | الإمارات |\n| England / America | إنجلترا / أمريكا |\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~6 min.** Play twice; learners catch *Where are you from?* + *I'm from…* and the *she's from…* report.\n\n---\n\n## 🧩 Decode it — القاعدة\n- **Question:** *Where are you from?* = إنت منين؟\n- **Answer:** *I'm from + (country).* → *I'm from Egypt.*\n- **Talking about others (to be extended):**\n  - *He's from ___* (هو من…) · *She's from ___* (هي من…)\n- **Nationality (خفيف):** country **Egypt** → nationality **Egyptian**. *I'm Egyptian.*\n\n> ملاحظة: مع الدول زي **the UAE** بنقول **the**. مع أغلب الدول (Egypt, Saudi Arabia) من غير *the*.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~6 min.** Teach Q→A + *he's/she's from*. Introduce **only one** nationality (*Egyptian*) — don't overload; nationalities are irregular (A1 = the pattern, not the list).\n\n---\n\n## 🗡️ Your Arsenal — ذخيرتك\n\n| English | بالعربي | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Where are you from? | إنت منين؟ | *— Where are you from? — I'm from Egypt.* |\n| I'm from… | أنا من… | *I'm from Cairo.* |\n| He's / She's from… | هو/هي من… | *She's from the UAE.* |\n| Egyptian | مصري | *I'm Egyptian.* |\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Accent Lab — معمل النطق\n**Target: the American /r/ in *from* and *are*.**\n- الـ /r/ الأمريكاني: اللسان **مقوّس لورا**، **من غير تكرار** (مش راء عربية مكررة).\n- **Stress the country:** *\"I'm from **E**gypt.\"* (الضغط على اسم البلد).\n\n> 🎧 **Record & compare:** قول *\"Where are you from? — I'm from Egypt.\"* → قارن الـ /r/ والضغط على البلد.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Drill American /r/ (from, are, Saudi Arabia). Watch for a trilled Arabic ر. Stress the country name.\n\n---\n\n## 🏋️ Train — تدرّب\n\n**Exercise 1 — Complete:**\n1. — Where ______ you from? — I'm ______ Egypt.\n2. This is Omar. ______ from Alexandria.\n3. This is Nour. ______ from the UAE.\n\n**Exercise 2 — True for you:**\n- Where are you from? → __________________\n\n**Exercise 3 — Match the country to *the*:**\n| Country | the? (نعم/لا) |\n|---|---|\n| Egypt | ______ |\n| UAE | ______ |\n| Saudi Arabia | ______ |\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~5 min.** Pair-check.\n> **Answers — Ex1:** *are / from* · *He's* · *She's*. **Ex3:** Egypt → لا · UAE → نعم (the UAE) · Saudi Arabia → لا.\n\n---\n\n## 🎤 Your Turn — دورك\nاسأل زميلين **\"Where are you from?\"**، بعدين **report** للمجموعة:\n- *\"This is ___. He's/She's from ___.\"*\n\n> 🎙️ **Record one exchange** (your question + their answer + your report). 👑\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Pairs ask + report to the group; record one.\n> **Success check:** correct question + answer with clear country stress; correct *he's/she's from* in the report.\n\n---\n\n## 📜 Your Orders — مهمتك\n- Post: *\"Hi, I'm ___. I'm from ___.\"* — and reply to a classmate saying where **they're** from (*\"You're from ___!\"*).\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Remember — افتكر\n- **Where are you from? → I'm from ___.**\n- Others: **He's/She's from ___.**\n- One nationality: **Egyptian**. Clear American **/r/**.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Self-check — صحّح لنفسك\n- **Ex1:** are · from · He's · She's\n- **Ex3:** Egypt → no · the UAE → yes · Saudi Arabia → no\n\n---\n\n*Empire English 👑 — الاستمرار أهم من الشدّة.*\n","s0-u1-l04":"# \"What Do You Do?\" — Jobs\n\n**Empire English** · Stage 0 — **Recruit** (A1) · Unit 1 · **Lesson 4**\n⏱️ ~30 min · 📹 Recorded + live · Prerequisite: L03\n*Built from: `curriculum/stage0/unit1-introducing-yourself.md` · **S0-U1-L04***\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **At a glance (~30 min):** Warm-up 4 · Input 6 · Decode 6 · Accent Lab 4 · Train 5 · Your Turn 4 · Orders — · Review 1.\n> **Objectives:** ask/answer *What do you do?* · use **a/an** with jobs · talk about others' jobs (*She's a doctor*).\n> **Support:** give the a/an rule card. **Stretch:** *I'm a student and I want to be an engineer.*\n> **Arabic ~60%.**\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Your Conquest — هدفك\nBy the end, **you'll be able to:**\n- Ask and answer **\"What do you do?\"** → **\"I'm a/an ___.\"**\n- Use **a / an** correctly with jobs.\n- Talk about someone's job: **\"She's a doctor.\"**\n\n> هتسأل وترد على *\"What do you do?\"*، وتستخدم **a / an** صح مع الوظايف، وتتكلم عن شغل حد تاني.\n\n---\n\n## 👑 Why this matters — ليه ده مهم\nدي اللبنة الأخيرة في التعريف بنفسك: الشغل. بعد الدرس ده تقدر تعرّف نفسك كامل: **name + country + job.**\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Warm-up — سخّن (افتكر)\nافتكر: *\"I'm ___, I'm from ___.\"* (من L02–L03).\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Rapid recall of name + country from L02–L03.\n\n---\n\n## 👂 Watch & Listen — اسمع وشوف\n> **A:** What do you do?\n> **B:** I'm a teacher. And you?\n> **A:** I'm an engineer.\n> **B:** My sister is a doctor.\n\n**Jobs (gloss):**\n\n| English | بالعربي |\n|---|---|\n| teacher / engineer | مدرّس / مهندس |\n| doctor / nurse | دكتور / ممرضة |\n| student / driver / accountant | طالب / سواق / محاسب |\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~6 min.** Play twice; catch *What do you do?* → *I'm a/an ___* and *a* vs *an*.\n\n---\n\n## 🧩 Decode it — القاعدة\n- **Question:** *What do you do?* = بتشتغل إيه؟\n- **Answer:** *I'm **a** / **an** + (job).*\n- **قاعدة a / an:**\n  - **a** قبل صوت ساكن → *a teacher, a doctor, a student.*\n  - **an** قبل صوت متحرك (a, e, i, o, u) → *an engineer, an accountant.*\n- **Others:** *He's a driver.* / *She's a doctor.*\n\n> ⚠️ ماتنساش الـ **a/an**! *\"I engineer\"* ❌ → *\"I'm an engineer\"* ✅.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~6 min, in Arabic.** Teach *What do you do?* + a/an rule (consonant vs vowel **sound**). **Watch for:** omitting the article (*\"I engineer\"*) — the key error to fix, gently + repeatedly.\n\n---\n\n## 🗡️ Your Arsenal — ذخيرتك\n\n| English | بالعربي | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| What do you do? | بتشتغل إيه؟ | *— What do you do? — I'm a nurse.* |\n| I'm a / an … | أنا (وظيفة) | *I'm an engineer.* |\n| He's / She's a … | هو/هي (وظيفة) | *She's a doctor.* |\n| a teacher / an engineer | مدرّس / مهندس | *a* + ساكن · *an* + متحرك |\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Accent Lab — معمل النطق\n**Target: linking *a/an* + the job, and stressing the job.**\n- *\"a teacher\"* → اربطهم: **a‿teacher**. *\"an engineer\"* → **an‿engineer**.\n- **Stress the job word:** *\"I'm an en**gi**neer.\"*\n\n> 🎧 **Record & compare:** قول *\"a teacher\"* و *\"an engineer\"* → قارن الربط والضغط.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Drill *a teacher / an engineer* linking; stress the job. Keep the /aɪ/ + /m/ from L02 clean.\n\n---\n\n## 🏋️ Train — تدرّب\n\n**Exercise 1 — a or an?**\n1. I'm ___ doctor.\n2. She's ___ accountant.\n3. He's ___ student.\n4. I'm ___ engineer.\n\n**Exercise 2 — Answer for you:**\n- What do you do? → __________________\n\n**Exercise 3 — Report (about others):**\n1. (Omar / driver) → __________________\n2. (Sara / doctor) → __________________\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~5 min.** Pair-check.\n> **Answers — Ex1:** a · an · a · an. **Ex3:** *He's a driver.* · *She's a doctor.*\n\n---\n\n## 🎤 Your Turn — دورك\nاسأل زميل **\"What do you do?\"**، رد، بعدين **report** عن حد تاني:\n- *\"I'm a/an ___. He's/She's a/an ___.\"*\n\n> 🎙️ **Record it.** دلوقتي عندك كل لبنات التعريف بنفسك. 👑\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Ask/answer/report; record one.\n> **Success check:** correct *I'm a/an + job* with the right article.\n\n---\n\n## 📜 Your Orders — مهمتك\n- Post: *\"I'm a/an ___.\"* + one classmate's job (*\"___ is a/an ___.\"*).\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Remember — افتكر\n- **What do you do? → I'm a/an ___.**\n- **a** + ساكن · **an** + متحرك.\n- Never drop the article: *I'm an engineer* ✅.\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Self-check — صحّح لنفسك\n- **Ex1:** a · an · a · an\n- **Ex3:** *He's a driver.* · *She's a doctor.*\n\n---\n\n*Empire English 👑 — small wins compound. You can now introduce yourself fully.*\n","s0-u1-l05":"# Unit Speaking Task: Introduce Yourself (+ Review)\n\n**Empire English** · Stage 0 — **Recruit** (A1) · Unit 1 · **Lesson 5**\n⏱️ ~30 min · 📹 Recorded + live (milestone) · Prerequisite: L01–L04\n*Built from: `curriculum/stage0/unit1-introducing-yourself.md` · **S0-U1-L05***\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **At a glance (~30 min):** Warm-up 5 · Model 4 · Notice 4 · Accent clinic 4 · Rehearse 6 · Record 4 · Feedback 2 · Quiz/celebrate 1.\n> **Objectives:** connected self-intro (greeting + name + country + job, 4–6 sentences) · ask another person · **record the Unit-1 milestone**.\n> **Support:** 4 sentences with the checklist card. **Stretch:** add *I live in…* / *Nice to meet you.*\n> **Arabic ~50%** (fading). **This recording is a key proof asset** — it pairs with the graduation clip later. Make the milestone feel big.\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 Your Conquest — هدفك (milestone)\nBy the end, **you'll be able to:**\n- Give a **connected self-introduction** (4–6 sentences): greeting + name + country + job.\n- Ask another person the same.\n- **Record your Unit-1 self-introduction** — your first real milestone. 👑\n\n> النهاردة هتجمّع كل لبنات الوحدة في تعريف واحد متصل، وتسجّله كـ **milestone**. قارنه بعدين بالـ Day-1 clip بتاعك وشوف الفرق.\n\n---\n\n## 🔁 Warm-up — سخّن (سلسلة سريعة)\nافتكر بسرعة كسلسلة: **greeting → name → from → job.**\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~5 min.** Rapid retrieval chain around the room: greeting, name, country, job — one each, fast.\n\n---\n\n## 👂 Watch & Listen — النموذج (Model)\nاسمع النموذج ده (5 جمل):\n> Hello! My name is Nour. I'm from Egypt — I'm from Cairo. I'm a pharmacist. Nice to meet you!\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Play a clean 5-sentence model. Learners just listen for the shape.\n\n---\n\n## 🧩 The Checklist — تشيك ليست التعريف الكويس\nتعريف كويس فيه:\n1. ✅ **Greeting** (Hello / Hi + time of day)\n2. ✅ **Name** (My name is… / I'm…)\n3. ✅ **Country** (I'm from…)\n4. ✅ **Job** (I'm a/an…)\n5. ⭐ **One extra** (Nice to meet you / I live in…)\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Break the model into these 5 boxes; give each learner the checklist card.\n\n---\n\n## 🎙️ Accent Lab — عيادة النطق (clinic)\nكل واحد يدرّب **أضعف صوت** عنده من الوحدة:\n- /h/ (hello, how) · /aɪ/ + /m/ (I'm) · American /r/ (from) · a/an linking · stress on the key word.\n\n> 🎧 **Record & compare** your weakest one before the milestone.\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min.** Personalized: each learner drills their **one** flagged weak sound from U0–U1.\n\n---\n\n## 🎤 Your Turn — التسجيل (the milestone)\nسجّل تعريف بنفسك كامل ومتصل (4–6 جمل): **greeting + name + country + job + one extra.**\n\n> 🎙️ **Record your Unit-1 self-introduction and save it.** ده الـ milestone بتاعك — أول دليل على تقدمك. احتفل بيه! 👑\n\n> [!TEACHER]\n> **~4 min record + 2 min feedback.** Rehearse with the checklist + a peer, then record.\n> **Success check (Unit-1 formative):** a connected 4–6 sentence self-intro, intelligible, correct *to be* + *a/an* (rubric: Fluency + Accuracy + Pronunciation at A1). Give warm, group-level feedback.\n\n---\n\n## 📜 Your Orders — مهمتك\n- **Post your self-introduction video/voice note** in the community.\n- **Complete the Unit-1 quiz.**\n- **Celebrate** — you finished your first EEC unit. 🎉\n\n---\n\n## 🧠 Remember — افتكر (Unit 1 wrap)\n- Greet → Name → From → Job → (extra).\n- Always use **I'm** and **a/an**.\n- Clear **/h/**, **/aɪ/**, American **/r/**; stress the key word.\n- *(كل ده هيرجع في Unit 2 warm-ups و Unit 10 review.)*\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Self-check — Unit 1 mini-quiz (صحّح لنفسك)\n1. Choose: *I ___ a teacher.* (am / is / are) → **am**\n2. a or an? *I'm ___ engineer.* → **an**\n3. Complete: *Where ___ you from?* → **are**\n4. Match: *How are you?* → **I'm fine, thanks.**\n\n---\n\n*Empire English 👑 — You've laid the first stones of your Empire. لبنة كل يوم، والإمبراطورية بتتبني.*\n"};
